How do you trouble shoot if aks deployment failed in production environment ? And how you handle this ? 
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Coming to aks deployments 
If pipeline failed in production environment 
Instead of rerun the pipeline i would check the pipeline status 
Here in pipeline logs i identify in which stage the pipeline is failing whether it is failing in build or docker image creation or pushing to acr or scanning the image or aks deployment 
If this is not is issue I will check the image is pushed to acr and check the image name and tag 
Or I will check the authentication used by the pipeline whether spn secret is expired or not 
If deployment failing I will connect to the cluster and with the help of kubectl commands I will find the logs and describe to check tha errors ...
Image pull back off - unable to pull image from acr by image name or tag or acr authentication 
Crashloopbackoff - due to database connection or missing env variable or resource limit 
If it is deployed but application is not accessible then we need to check service and ingress, lb and endpoints 
If it is causing more time to debugging then instead of delay we can rollback to previous successful version 
After understanding the root cause need to documention to avoid in further 
This is the approach I follow when aks deployments failure in production environment.

